# PHP Rules

## Standards
- PHP 8.4+, PSR-12 coding style
- PHP-CS-Fixer config: short arrays, ordered imports, single quotes, trailing commas in multiline
- `declare(strict_types=1)` in new files

## Naming
- Classes, interfaces: PascalCase. Interfaces have `Interface` suffix
- Methods and functions: camelCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Variables: `$camelCase`
- Endpoint files: snake_case (`get_jobs.php`), class files: PascalCase (`RemotiveFetcher.php`)

## Forbidden
- No string interpolation in SQL — use prepared statements
- No `mysql_*` or `mysqli_*` — PDO only
- No `extract()` — explicit variable assignment only
- No `eval()` or `assert()` for code execution
- No die/exit outside of respondJson
- No dynamic class or function calls

## Patterns
- API endpoints: validate → sanitize → execute → respondJson
- CRON jobs: guard with CRON_SECRET_KEY, log to sync_log
- Migrations: idempotent with information_schema guards, zero-padded filenames
